 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Salih: no motif. The killing of the she-camel and the earthquake are not drawn (night sky, no motif in 77-79). Their challenge (77:7-15) is framed «على سبيل الاستهزاء». Light only for the believers' answer (75:19). 79:11-14 avoids Al-Muyassar's «شيطان رجيم» (Quran wording). STAGING v4: c1 (75-76): a mountain valley; the arrogant chiefs (three faceless men in dark robes) speak to the weak who believed (two figures in light robes: few, and not a crowd); Salih is named but not drawn here (neither verse places him in the scene). The chiefs ask (75:1, 75:12) and point at the believers they address (75:14), the believers answer (75:18) with a light plate (75:19-23) and a soft sparkle on 75:23 (believers); the chiefs answer (76:1), shake their heads (76:6) and turn away on 76:8 (disbelievers). c2 (77-79): the she-camel is never drawn in this video, and nothing moves or gestures on 77:1-2 (the hamstringing is not shown in any way); the camera holds wide, then on the chiefs for their insolence (77:3), they speak their challenge to Salih (77:7, the drop on the left), turn away on 77:11 (bring us what you promise; no gesture inside the conditional 77:12-15) and leave on 77:15 with Salih's drop, so the stage is empty before 78:1. The quake falls on the empty valley (78:2 to 79:1): no person, no body, no ruin; day (no dawn or low red sun over the punishment). 79: Salih's drop appears again on 79:1, turns away (79:2) and speaks to them after their end (79:3, As-Sa'di: a rebuke after Allah destroyed them); a seal plate for the message of his Lord (79:6-8)."
 },
